            <ArticleTitle>Pylephlebitis due to perforated diverticulitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>229-30</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pylephlebitis or septic thrombophlebitis of the portal vein is an uncommon and frequently fatal complication of diverticulitis. We describe a case report of a patient with pylephlebitis due to a perforation of the sigmoid. The patient was successfully treated with broad spectrum antibiotics and a Hartmann procedure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
